  "_range_comment": "range_low/range_high are the REFERENCE range - what a normal result looks like, used for flagging. plausible_min/plausible_max are the PHYSIOLOGIC range - the limits outside which a value is not a result but an artifact. The two are unrelated and must not be conflated: total cholesterol has a reference range of 0-200 because the clinical convention is '<200', yet a serum cholesterol of 0 is impossible. An earlier version of the generator clamped drawn values at 0.0, which manufactured a spike of exactly-zero troponins, CRPs and cholesterols - values a real analyser reports as 'below detection limit' (a NULL), never as a number. Draws are now clamped into the plausible range, and genuinely-unresulted tests are NULL.",
  "_specimen_comment": "specimens/methods constrain the sibling-code expansion in expansion.py, which previously took the naive cross-product of every analyte with every specimen and every method and so emitted 'Systolic blood pressure, cerebrospinal fluid, immunoassay'. An empty list means the analyte takes no variant on that axis - vitals are not drawn from a specimen at all."
}
